Navi48Bringup — Phase 3 GPU bring-up kext for Navi 48 (gfx1201) on x86 macOS.

This work reuses and adapts code from two upstream projects, with thanks:

* RDNA4FB  (BSD 3-Clause, (c) 2026 Sunneva N. Mariu / somestupidgirl)
  https://github.com/somestupidgirl/RDNA4FB
  - src/ipdiscovery.{hpp,cpp} are used verbatim (their BSD-3 headers retained).
  - The BAR5 register-mapping, indirect-VRAM (MM_INDEX/MM_DATA), on-die IP
    discovery, and read-only PSP/SMU survey techniques are ported from it.

* mac-amdgpu  (MIT, lemonade-sdk)
  https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/mac-amdgpu
  - The IP-block bring-up sequences (gfx/gmc/psp/smu/sdma/mes/ih v12/v14/v7)
    that later writing stages will port are derived from this project, which
    proved the full Navi 48 bring-up on macOS (Apple Silicon / DriverKit).

Register semantics are cross-checked against the Linux amdgpu driver
(drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu), GPL-2.0 — used as documentation/reference only,
no GPL code is copied into this permissively-licensed kext.
